#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186092040 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "84a533e8-9a7c-58f3-9d3c-7c08b3c6bfd1" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Arc Length of a Polar Curve"}] :question/id #uuid "57034318-5a6e-53f6-a8d3-ae8c61692947" :question/math-academy-id "e-641" :question/problem "Find the arc length of the polar curve $r=2(1-\\cos\\theta)$ for $0 \\leq \\theta \\leq \\pi$ (shown in blue in the picture above).\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/999/Source/Images/7b8c89d9e599587ac6274b08d6202514.png)" :question/worked-solution "The arc length $L$ of a polar curve $r=r(\\theta)$ is given by\n\n$$\nL = \\int_{\\theta_1}^{\\theta_2} \\sqrt{r^2 +\\left(\\frac{\\textrm{d}r}{\\textrm{d}\\theta}\\right)^2}\\,\\textrm{d}\\theta\n$$\n\nSince\n\n$$\nr=2(1-\\cos\\theta)\n$$\n\nwe have\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\textrm{d}r}{\\textrm{d}\\theta} = 2\\sin\\theta\n$$\n\nTherefore, the arc length is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nL &= ∫_{θ_{1}}^{θ_{2}}\\sqrt{r^{2} + (\\frac{dr}{dθ})^{2}}dθ \\\\\n&= ∫_{0}^{π}\\sqrt{(2 - 2\\cos θ)^{2} + (2\\sin θ)^{2}}dθ \\\\\n&= ∫_{0}^{π}\\sqrt{4 - 8\\cos θ + 4\\cos^{2} θ + 4\\sin^{2} θ}dθ \\\\\n&= ∫_{0}^{π}\\sqrt{4 - 8\\cos θ + 4}dθ \\\\\n&= ∫_{0}^{π}\\sqrt{8 - 8\\cos θ}dθ \\\\\n&= 2\\sqrt{2}∫_{0}^{π}\\sqrt{1 - \\cos θ}dθ\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe now use the half-angle formula\n\n$$\n1-\\cos\\theta =2\\sin^2\\left(\\dfrac{\\theta}{2}\\right)\n$$\n\nto give\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nL &= 2\\sqrt{2}∫_{0}^{π}\\sqrt{2\\sin^{2} (\\frac{θ}{2})}dθ \\\\\n&= 2\\sqrt{2} \\cdot \\sqrt{2} \\cdot ∫_{0}^{π}\\sin (\\frac{θ}{2})dθ \\\\\n&=-4 \\cdot 2(\\cos (\\frac{θ}{2})) \\mid _{0}^{π} \\\\\n&=-8(\\cos (\\frac{π}{2}) - \\cos 0) \\\\\n&=-8(0 - 1) \\\\\n&= 8\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186092070 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "cd0b4da9-1a0f-5a46-aff1-3ce5c0cebb3b" :knowledge-point/title "Creating an Integral Expression For the Arc Length of a Polar Curve"}] :question/id #uuid "8b8e3c66-fc60-57ac-baf7-0661e213d01e" :question/math-academy-id "e-7400" :question/problem "Find an integral expression for the arc length of the polar curve $r=3-\\sin(7\\theta)$ for $0 \\leq \\theta \\leq \\pi$, shown in blue in the diagram above.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/999/Source/Images/9a98033ef7124397b87e336d2d7778e9.png)" :question/worked-solution "The arc length $L$ of a polar curve $r=r(\\theta)$ is given by\n\n$$\nL = \\int_{\\theta_1}^{\\theta_2} \\sqrt{r^2 +\\left(\\frac{\\textrm{d}r}{\\textrm{d}\\theta}\\right)^2}\\,\\textrm{d}\\theta\n$$\n\nSince\n\n$$\nr=3-\\sin(7\\theta)\n$$\n\nwe have\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\textrm{d}r}{\\textrm{d}\\theta} =-7\\cos(7\\theta)\n$$\n\nTherefore, the arc length is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nL &= ∫_{θ_{1}}^{θ_{2}}\\sqrt{r^{2} + (\\frac{dr}{dθ})^{2}}dθ \\\\\n&= ∫_{0}^{π}\\sqrt{(3 - \\sin (7θ))^{2} + (-7\\cos (7θ))^{2}}dθ \\\\\n&= ∫_{0}^{π}\\sqrt{9 - 6\\sin (7θ) + \\sin^{2} (7θ) + 49\\cos^{2} (7θ)}dθ \\\\\n&= ∫_{0}^{π}\\sqrt{9 - 6\\sin (7θ) + \\sin^{2} (7θ) + \\cos^{2} (7θ) + 48\\cos^{2} (7θ)}dθ \\\\\n&= ∫_{0}^{π}\\sqrt{9 - 6\\sin (7θ) + 1 + 48\\cos^{2} (7θ)}dθ \\\\\n&= ∫_{0}^{π}\\sqrt{10 - 6\\sin (7θ) + 48\\cos^{2} (7θ)}dθ\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186092869 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "84a533e8-9a7c-58f3-9d3c-7c08b3c6bfd1" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Arc Length of a Polar Curve"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b6064233-ed38-5ef3-8349-1dd3a03c75b5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{π}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186091680} {:answer/id #uuid "db306417-a82a-5664-b0d9-2362a93d761e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2π}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186091681} {:answer/id #uuid "0f1e274f-8eb5-5481-b78c-b5fbba99795e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "π" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186091682} {:answer/id #uuid "6c96387a-f2f3-5c59-a3a3-92a83acc5088" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2π" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186091683} {:answer/id #uuid "74a7db6a-2d70-5ff8-b64d-297fa28f56d0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3π}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186091684}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "db306417-a82a-5664-b0d9-2362a93d761e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2π}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186091681} :answer-field/id #uuid "e1c56fba-9bc3-51b4-a438-d20c93c6b9e0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186091679}] :question/id #uuid "dfaa6223-b113-5398-adeb-e8d8b6d36965" :question/math-academy-id "q-9532" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/999/Source/Images/q-9532.png)\n\nFind the arc length of the polar curve $r = 2\\sin θ$ for $\\frac{π}{2} \\le θ \\le \\frac{5π}{6}$ (shown in blue in the diagram above)."}]}
